WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.800
It's normal to worry about the legal side of helping, but good Samaritan laws are generally there to protect you as long as you act in good faith.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:16.900
These laws exist in every state to support people who step up, though the specific details can vary, so it's always a good idea to be familiar with your local rules.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:20.700
Always prioritize your own safety and skills when deciding to act.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:25.600
If you do choose to assist, you must stay with the person until professional help arrives.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:34.299
While providing care, please protect their privacy by sharing information only with EMS and keeping personal details or photos off of social media.

00:00:34.299 --> 00:00:36.700
Stick to the skills you are trained for today.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:42.099
If you are asked to do something beyond your certification, politely decline and wait for the pros.

00:00:42.099 --> 00:00:45.599
Always ask an alert person for verbal consent before you start.

00:00:45.599 --> 00:00:54.700
If a conscious person refuses your help, you must respect that choice, though you should still call 911 if it is a life-threatening emergency and document the refusal.

